WEBVTT

00:01:47.970 --> 00:01:53.100
Get... away from here...

00:02:03.790 --> 00:02:06.730
You've really gotten good 
at maintenance, you have.

00:02:07.020 --> 00:02:10.520
I've put in enough imagery 
coolant for another 6 bells.

00:02:12.810 --> 00:02:16.650
I've got some nice leaves for us 
to have a drink together with.

00:02:17.210 --> 00:02:19.390
Let's have tea, Lugh.

00:02:21.810 --> 00:02:23.910
Sure, Grandpa.

00:02:27.700 --> 00:02:32.040
Wilderness Imagery Lighthouse

00:02:41.680 --> 00:02:44.220
Lugh, you're a natural.

00:02:44.470 --> 00:02:46.210
It's quite something.

00:02:46.210 --> 00:02:50.220
I suppose it's because you were raised here 
in this wilderness imagery lighthouse.

00:02:50.220 --> 00:02:53.480
You may have been born to become 
this imagery lighthouse's keeper.

00:02:53.480 --> 00:02:54.980
You're a lot like me.

00:02:55.230 --> 00:02:57.690
You're my treasure.

00:02:57.690 --> 00:02:59.700
Stop it, Grandpa.

00:03:00.250 --> 00:03:04.760
I want to hurry and become the 
imagery lighthouse keeper like you,

00:03:04.760 --> 00:03:07.940
but you won't even let me stabilize the light.

00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:11.950
Now, now... All in due time.

00:03:11.950 --> 00:03:13.540
There is no need to be in such a hurry.

00:03:15.920 --> 00:03:17.240
Lugh...

00:03:19.010 --> 00:03:21.200
The wind is strong today...

00:03:22.060 --> 00:03:23.520
What is the matter, Lugh?

00:03:24.300 --> 00:03:26.740
Lately something has been odd.

00:03:27.110 --> 00:03:30.850
I feel like there's someone besides 
us in the imagery lighthouse.

00:03:30.850 --> 00:03:32.720
What? An intruder?

00:03:32.720 --> 00:03:34.090
Where did you see them?

00:03:34.090 --> 00:03:35.960
No, it's not that.

00:03:35.960 --> 00:03:42.700
It's that a person... Or 
rather, I sense something...

00:03:42.700 --> 00:03:47.830
It's like it's not some living 
creature of this world...

00:03:48.570 --> 00:03:49.890
Oh?

00:03:50.140 --> 00:03:52.620
I thought it was real, but you're 
just telling ghost stories.

00:03:52.620 --> 00:03:56.030
Something like that isn't going to spook me.

00:03:56.030 --> 00:03:57.350
That's not it!

00:03:57.350 --> 00:04:00.050
I can't really make it out 
well, but I can hear its voice!

00:04:02.760 --> 00:04:07.080
I hear something like, "Get away from here..."

00:04:07.330 --> 00:04:08.390
Lugh.

00:04:09.800 --> 00:04:13.190
Don't even joke about something as sad as that.

00:04:14.110 --> 00:04:20.190
This Liquid Sand River is plagued by 
sandstorms, and the only folk who come here are Bees.

00:04:21.110 --> 00:04:26.950
We spend our entire lives living inside the 
tower to protect the imagery lighthouse.

00:04:28.100 --> 00:04:31.950
Your mother and father could 
not stand it and left here.

00:04:32.530 --> 00:04:36.440
Lugh, you are the only one left to me.

00:04:37.190 --> 00:04:38.960
Grandpa...

00:04:39.560 --> 00:04:46.430
Being the imagery lighthouse keeper is proud 
work as a lifeline for the travelers between cities.

00:04:47.840 --> 00:04:53.230
But if you leave, I can no 
longer continue it on my own.

00:04:53.810 --> 00:04:56.020
I'm not going anywhere!

00:04:56.020 --> 00:04:58.390
Don't look so sad, Grandpa.

00:04:58.760 --> 00:05:00.120
I see.

00:05:00.120 --> 00:05:02.010
Then all is well.

00:05:02.700 --> 00:05:06.700
Well, I must go write the journal for the day.

00:05:06.700 --> 00:05:09.500
Go to bed now, Lugh.

00:05:16.920 --> 00:05:19.060
What a strong wind...

00:05:19.060 --> 00:05:22.100
The purple iron on the plate-glass 
windows is rattling...

00:05:22.100 --> 00:05:25.150
Like the voice of some living thing...

00:05:25.150 --> 00:05:27.630
Get away from here...

00:05:43.570 --> 00:05:46.150
I fell asleep after passing out from shock...

00:05:46.970 --> 00:05:48.940
What the heck was that?

00:05:50.450 --> 00:05:53.890
Maybe I'm going crazy...

00:05:57.100 --> 00:05:59.540
Grandpa, I've brought you hot water!

00:05:59.540 --> 00:06:01.700
Lugh? I'm upstairs.

00:06:01.700 --> 00:06:03.370
The journal again?

00:06:03.370 --> 00:06:05.920
You sure write a lot in it.

00:06:13.150 --> 00:06:16.930
Grandpa, are these all the daily journals?

00:06:18.630 --> 00:06:22.400
Oh, right... You've never come 
into this room before, Lugh.

00:06:22.970 --> 00:06:27.030
These journals are my life itself.

00:06:27.650 --> 00:06:30.700
Now, come here, and we'll make tea.

00:06:31.590 --> 00:06:36.640
I've got some nice leaves 
here to drink with you.

00:06:36.640 --> 00:06:37.390
Sure!

00:06:48.900 --> 00:06:50.840
What are these bruises?

00:06:52.090 --> 00:06:54.280
What could...

00:06:54.280 --> 00:06:57.350
I feel like there's something 
I should remember...

00:06:59.660 --> 00:07:02.050
Weird, I suddenly feel cold...

00:07:18.100 --> 00:07:19.700
Grand...pa?

00:07:40.850 --> 00:07:42.220
Hate...

00:07:42.220 --> 00:07:43.540
Want to kill...

00:07:43.540 --> 00:07:44.660
Hate...

00:07:44.660 --> 00:07:45.690
Hate...

00:07:47.830 --> 00:07:49.080
Hate...

00:07:49.370 --> 00:07:50.580
Hate...

00:07:50.850 --> 00:07:52.000
Hate...

00:07:53.660 --> 00:07:54.820
Grandpa?

00:07:55.370 --> 00:07:57.090
Hate...

00:07:57.090 --> 00:07:58.150
Hate...

00:07:58.640 --> 00:07:59.810
Hate...

00:08:03.100 --> 00:08:04.350
Wait...

00:08:05.150 --> 00:08:06.350
I...

00:08:06.350 --> 00:08:07.250
I...

00:08:08.140 --> 00:08:10.100
I don't have a grandpa!

00:08:11.700 --> 00:08:14.550
How long have I been here?

00:08:15.730 --> 00:08:17.100
You are...

00:08:18.470 --> 00:08:20.010
Who are you?

00:08:22.180 --> 00:08:23.710
Lag...

00:08:30.900 --> 00:08:34.820
So, have you written that 
Dear Gauche letter yet?

00:08:34.820 --> 00:08:36.070
No.

00:08:36.070 --> 00:08:39.980
I tried a picture letter, but 
my drawings are terrible.

00:08:41.020 --> 00:08:45.210
Lag, you haven't met the express 
delivery Bee yet, have you?

00:08:45.830 --> 00:08:48.950
Jiggy Pepper? No, not yet.

00:08:48.950 --> 00:08:52.710
But I met Jiggy-san's little 
sister in the town of Kyrie.

00:08:53.080 --> 00:08:54.080
Little sister?

00:08:54.080 --> 00:08:55.080
He has a little sister?

00:08:55.640 --> 00:09:01.450
It seems like Jiggy-san is passing through 
Liquid Sand River today in Northwest Yuusari.

00:09:01.450 --> 00:09:02.480
Liquid?

00:09:02.730 --> 00:09:06.300
I'm going on a delivery to a town 
in that direction right now.

00:09:06.300 --> 00:09:10.450
You almost never meet the guy. Why 
don't you stretch your legs a little?

00:09:10.450 --> 00:09:13.340
He might be able to give you some advice.

00:09:13.340 --> 00:09:15.860
Jiggy-san's totally cool!

00:09:15.860 --> 00:09:18.130
And especially that iron horse of his!

00:09:18.130 --> 00:09:22.080
It's fueled by heart, just like a shindan.

00:09:22.080 --> 00:09:24.300
Man, I wish I could give it a ride!

00:09:24.570 --> 00:09:29.050
You can't because you'd have to use your 
heart for an extended period of time.

00:09:29.050 --> 00:09:31.170
Not possible for Zazie the hothead.

00:09:31.170 --> 00:09:32.420
Shut it, Connor!

00:09:35.000 --> 00:09:36.820
If I didn't have a delivery...

00:09:36.820 --> 00:09:38.800
I'd go see him myself.

00:09:40.910 --> 00:09:43.330
That's right... I'm...

00:09:43.330 --> 00:09:44.300
Lag!

00:09:45.050 --> 00:09:47.480
Lag, get away from here!

00:09:48.440 --> 00:09:49.400
Niche?

00:09:52.050 --> 00:09:54.940
You abandoned this honorable job...

00:09:54.940 --> 00:09:56.740
Why did you leave?

00:09:57.450 --> 00:10:00.030
My grandson was my treasure...

00:10:00.780 --> 00:10:03.870
Why did you take him away from me?

00:10:09.170 --> 00:10:11.790
The pages from the imagery 
lighthouse keeper's journal?

00:10:13.800 --> 00:10:18.500
I see, so that's what is 
overflowing within this tower...

00:10:20.540 --> 00:10:23.400
The heart contained in these journals, yes?

00:10:38.100 --> 00:10:39.820
Gaichuu Korona.

00:10:41.200 --> 00:10:44.200
It's time for desert.

00:10:51.650 --> 00:10:52.880
Gaichuu Korona.

00:10:53.690 --> 00:10:55.320
It's time for dessert.

00:10:56.440 --> 00:10:58.670
Shindan, Lapis Lazuli!

00:11:09.710 --> 00:11:12.060
Grandpa disappeared!

00:11:12.060 --> 00:11:13.090
Lag!

00:11:13.610 --> 00:11:16.100
It's breaking apart!

00:11:16.100 --> 00:11:17.280
It?

00:11:19.060 --> 00:11:22.100
That's the Gaichuu, Korona?

00:11:22.100 --> 00:11:24.280
And that light is a shindan!

00:11:24.280 --> 00:11:25.900
Who?

00:11:26.170 --> 00:11:29.000
What was I doing here?

00:11:29.000 --> 00:11:30.130
Lag!

00:11:32.950 --> 00:11:35.690
Why didn't you know it was me?

00:11:36.920 --> 00:11:42.330
I even tried licking you, biting you, dropping 
you, stomping on you, grabbing you, and dropping you!

00:11:42.330 --> 00:11:44.110
I-I'm sorry, Niche!

00:11:44.110 --> 00:11:46.440
And you dropped me twice?

00:11:50.290 --> 00:11:52.540
The building is collapsing.

00:11:52.540 --> 00:11:55.310
Let's get out of here for now, Niche.

00:12:00.100 --> 00:12:03.180
This is awful... The entire place is in ruins.

00:12:03.700 --> 00:12:04.700
That's right!

00:12:05.400 --> 00:12:10.000
I came to this Liquid Sand 
River to meet Jiggy-san...

00:12:11.650 --> 00:12:15.900
And on the top of the crumbling imagery 
lighthouse, I found the Gaichuu, Korona.

00:12:17.340 --> 00:12:20.570
To defeat the Gaichuu, I entered the tower.

00:12:20.570 --> 00:12:21.840
And in that instant...

00:12:33.660 --> 00:12:37.860
Huh? What was I doing again?

00:12:38.510 --> 00:12:39.810
That's right...

00:12:39.810 --> 00:12:42.490
I have to fix the coolant pipe.

00:13:02.450 --> 00:13:07.660
Get... away from here...

00:13:08.550 --> 00:13:14.570
Something from the imagery lighthouse 
caused me to hallucinate.

00:13:21.440 --> 00:13:23.610
Who exactly was that old man?

00:13:25.210 --> 00:13:27.060
He was making a fearsome face...

00:13:27.060 --> 00:13:29.560
He said, "Hate," again and again...

00:13:29.850 --> 00:13:32.330
I wonder who he was aiming the gun at?

00:13:38.550 --> 00:13:41.960
These journals are my life itself.

00:13:42.710 --> 00:13:45.840
Show me Grandpa's heart...

00:13:47.150 --> 00:13:48.300
Red Needle!

00:13:51.340 --> 00:13:55.600
I told you that these 
journals are my life itself.

00:13:58.820 --> 00:14:03.200
Ever since I became the imagery 
lighthouse keeper after my father...

00:14:03.970 --> 00:14:09.210
When I married your grandmother, 
when our son was born...

00:14:10.750 --> 00:14:15.900
When I lost my father, when 
my wife went before me...

00:14:18.050 --> 00:14:23.980
When my son was married, and 
when my grandson was born...

00:14:24.700 --> 00:14:27.900
I'm not going to take over this place.

00:14:28.430 --> 00:14:32.250
I'm going to become the imagery 
lighthouse keeper like you, Grandpa!

00:14:32.250 --> 00:14:35.570
I see! So, you'll be my successor?

00:14:35.570 --> 00:14:37.470
Right, Grandpa!

00:14:42.850 --> 00:14:46.650
And even when my son and his 
wife left with my grandson...

00:14:46.650 --> 00:14:50.650
I continued to keep the journal just like this.

00:15:00.840 --> 00:15:03.170
It's illegible now.

00:15:03.700 --> 00:15:06.240
I must rewrite it.

00:15:06.240 --> 00:15:07.380
Hate...

00:15:07.750 --> 00:15:09.040
Hate...

00:15:09.040 --> 00:15:11.590
Today my son and his wife left.

00:15:11.590 --> 00:15:14.730
Only my grandson and I are left.

00:15:14.730 --> 00:15:15.920
Hate...

00:15:15.920 --> 00:15:22.350
Starting today, the two of us, my grandson and I,
must protect this wilderness imagery lighthouse.

00:15:17.050 --> 00:15:18.300
Hate...

00:15:22.350 --> 00:15:23.260
Hate...

00:15:24.110 --> 00:15:25.450
Hate...

00:15:27.610 --> 00:15:32.240
I am so pleased that my grandson 
has pride in this job.

00:15:32.240 --> 00:15:33.300
Hate...

00:15:34.040 --> 00:15:35.400
Hate...

00:15:42.980 --> 00:15:45.840
He couldn't take the sadness all alone.

00:15:45.840 --> 00:15:50.090
In his journals, he continued weaving tales of 
his life together with a grandson who wasn't there.

00:15:50.350 --> 00:15:52.460
And he did his best to believe in them.

00:15:53.250 --> 00:15:56.850
To him, those false journals 
were what kept him going.

00:15:57.490 --> 00:15:59.720
They were letters to himself.

00:16:00.600 --> 00:16:04.980
But the heart that was contained 
within them was hatred.

00:16:05.230 --> 00:16:08.980
Y-You're Jiggy Pepper?!

00:16:09.970 --> 00:16:12.130
F-For real?

00:16:14.150 --> 00:16:17.030
The old man died a long time ago.

00:16:17.900 --> 00:16:21.100
With no-one to take it over, the imagery 
lighthouse has been closed down.

00:16:21.100 --> 00:16:23.540
And the journals inside left as they were...

00:16:24.320 --> 00:16:27.880
The Gaichuu ate the heart 
contained in the journals.

00:16:29.320 --> 00:16:33.000
Using the entire imagery lighthouse 
as an external stomach,

00:16:33.000 --> 00:16:35.930
it continued to consume a 
great quantity of heart.

00:16:37.250 --> 00:16:42.910
Your consciousness was probably lost in the 
overflowing heart inside the imagery lighthouse.

00:16:44.050 --> 00:16:45.090
But...

00:16:49.270 --> 00:16:52.910
It seems that it had no effect 
on your little dingo girl.

00:16:54.910 --> 00:16:57.520
Thanks to her, I was easily 
able to defeat the Korona.

00:16:57.520 --> 00:16:58.320
I appreciate it.

00:17:00.720 --> 00:17:02.040
Lag Seeing.

00:17:03.030 --> 00:17:07.350
You have the power to sense the 
heart stored within things, yes?

00:17:07.980 --> 00:17:11.340
But being engulfed in it unable 
to return is a sign of weakness.

00:17:12.890 --> 00:17:14.660
Right, Jiggy-san.

00:17:15.250 --> 00:17:17.820
I... I...

00:17:17.820 --> 00:17:21.380
Grandpa really loved me...

00:17:21.380 --> 00:17:23.140
He cared for me so...

00:17:23.560 --> 00:17:26.960
If I left, Grandpa would be so sad...

00:17:26.960 --> 00:17:28.110
Come...

00:17:28.110 --> 00:17:29.630
Let's pour some tea.

00:17:29.630 --> 00:17:31.610
I've got some excellent leaves.

00:17:32.160 --> 00:17:35.820
I want to have tea together with you.

00:17:37.510 --> 00:17:39.990
You are my treasure!

00:17:40.850 --> 00:17:42.160
Grandpa...

00:17:42.790 --> 00:17:46.500
Letters are a form that peoples' hearts take.

00:17:47.030 --> 00:17:51.010
But, there are also self-centered 
feelings that can take form.

00:17:51.330 --> 00:17:55.880
Remember well that not all letters 
consider the feelings of the recipient.

00:17:56.900 --> 00:17:59.590
Don't be taken in either 
by good intentions or bad.

00:18:00.060 --> 00:18:02.360
Become a Bee with your own strong heart.

00:18:08.180 --> 00:18:11.770
I've learned something new about letters.

00:18:12.570 --> 00:18:16.150
I'm sorry for causing you 
to be delayed, Jiggy-san.

00:18:16.150 --> 00:18:17.140
It's okay.

00:18:17.510 --> 00:18:19.940
I wanted to meet you as well.

00:18:21.290 --> 00:18:24.300
I received a letter from my sister in Kyrie.

00:18:25.350 --> 00:18:27.150
From Nelli?

00:18:27.430 --> 00:18:28.190
Yes.

00:18:33.430 --> 00:18:35.920
I'm thankful, Lag Seeing.

00:18:37.340 --> 00:18:39.590
You saved my sister.

00:18:39.930 --> 00:18:42.590
We are not going to forget that.

00:18:44.600 --> 00:18:46.560
Until we meet again, Lag.

00:18:51.810 --> 00:18:52.810
Right!

00:18:52.810 --> 00:18:55.860
Thank you very much, Jiggy-san!

00:19:02.810 --> 00:19:04.240
Seriously?!

00:19:04.240 --> 00:19:07.250
So like... So like, you rode it!?

00:19:08.050 --> 00:19:10.370
"Until we meet again, Lag."

00:19:11.600 --> 00:19:15.300
Man, what a cool customer!

00:19:14.090 --> 00:19:16.720
Sylvette, is dinner ready yet?

00:19:17.790 --> 00:19:18.860
Are you idiots?

00:19:26.040 --> 00:19:40.920
Next: Reverse World
